This test works by running on all possible permutations of the inputs. If the precondition is met, tests will run and the contract enforced. If not, the test will be bypassed. 

**Caveat: This only works for types that have built-in contracts. So for most ADTs (Abstract Data Types, e.g., Lists, Sets, Deques, and so on), it won't work.**

For more advanced analysis and fault localization, consider integrating Microsoft's Pex with Moq (an object mocking library for .NET). This will allow you to simulate the behavior of dependencies and provide rigorous coverage over your entire system.

